#: docs/app/content/guide/layout-and-navigation.mdx
msgid ""
"Set <0/> when the site's header or footer lives outside Ardo's layout, or when"
" the page should use normal document scrolling. Ardo keeps the existing "
"viewport shell by default. In document mode, the document scrolls, the sidebar"
" and page rail stick below the configured header height, and an external "
"footer remains reachable after the documentation content. The mode also "
"applies when <1/> replaces Ardo's default layout class. Since that prop still "
"replaces the default class, provide any root display or width rules your "
"custom layout needs."
msgstr ""
"<0/> sirve para cabeceras y pies externos o desplazamiento normal. El shell de"
" viewport sigue siendo el predeterminado. En modo documento, navegación y "
"panel se fijan bajo la altura de cabecera configurada; el pie externo sigue "
"accesible. También funciona con <1/> propia, que debe aportar las reglas de "
"visualización y anchura."

